      value: These bubbles are carbon dioxide - a waste gas your cells make when
        they use up oxygen. Your blood picks it up and carries it back to your lungs
        so you can breathe it out. Breathe in the good oxygen, breathe out the carbon
        dioxide!
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3117820576988222420, guid: 6a3606e324e18c94eafed99681c415b7, type: 3}
